column11:
I generally prefer:<p><pre><code>    var banana;
    if (!banana) babana = "banana";
</code></pre>
or<p><pre><code>    var banana;
    banana = banana || "banana";
</code></pre>
I have a strong dislike for implicit globals  even at the toplevel  and the global object isn't necessarily `window` (it's not in the Spidermonkey or Node shells for instance, I'm not sure it is in Web Workers  there's a WorkerGlobalScope object but i don't know if it's bound to a global called `window`).<p>If `undefined` has to be checked for explicitly (because `null` or `0` or `""` are valid values), check `banana === undefined` (or `banana === void 0` if your coworkers are assholes)
